index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5452b238e664a2222d64a45e583f55cc1f05f40a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-sku-shipping-vat-bugs/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+## Why
+
+Three reports show the code departing from the README business rules: lower-case SKUs are refused as unknown, an order at exactly €50.00 is charged shipping, and line VAT is rounded down instead of half up.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- SKU lookup in the catalogue canonicalises the SKU (trim and upper-case) instead of only trimming.
+- Free shipping applies when goods after every discount are 5000 cents or more (the check currently requires more than 5000).
+- Line VAT is rounded half up to the cent (it currently rounds down).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `sku-lookup`: SKUs are case-insensitive and trimmed when looked up.
+- `shipping`: free shipping threshold.
+- `vat`: per-line VAT rounding.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+(none: there are no existing specs under `openspec/specs/`)
+
+## Impact
+
+- README business rules affected: "Products" (SKUs case-insensitive), "Shipping" (free from €50.00), "VAT" (half-up per line). The README already states them correctly; **no README change**.
+- Code: `src/catalog.ts` (`find`), `src/shipping.ts` (`shippingCost`), `src/tax.ts` (`lineVat`); tests in `test/*.test.ts`.
+- Out of scope: any other rule, shipping bands, VAT rates, stock handling, and data already stored in past orders.
